@startuml Qualification_Management_SSD
title Sequence Diagram – US 2.2.13 “Register and Manage Qualifications”

actor "Logistics Operator" as Operator
boundary "QualificationsController\n(API Layer)" as Controller
control "QualificationService\n(Application Layer)" as Service
entity "QualificationMapper\n(Data Mapper)" as Mapper
entity "Qualification\n(Domain Entity)" as Qualification
entity "IQualificationRepository /\nQualificationRepository\n(Persistence Layer)" as Repo
database "Azure SQL Database\n(Infrastructure Layer)" as DB

' ===========================
' CONTEXT
' ===========================
note over Operator
User Story 2.2.13 – Register and Manage Qualifications

"As a Logistics Operator, I want to register and manage
qualifications (create, update), so that staff members and
resources can be associated with the correct skills."
end note

== CREATE QUALIFICATION ==

Operator -> Controller: POST /api/qualifications (QualificationDTO)
activate Controller

Controller -> Mapper: ToDomain(dto)
activate Mapper
Mapper --> Controller: Qualification
deactivate Mapper

Controller -> Service: RegisterQualificationAsync(code, name)
activate Service

Service -> Repo: GetByCodeAsync(code)
activate Repo
Repo --> Service: null (no existing qualification)
deactivate Repo

note over Service
Business Rules:
- Code must be unique
- Name must be descriptive and non-empty
end note

Service -> Repo: AddAsync(Qualification)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: INSERT INTO Qualifications (Code, Name)
activate DB
DB --> Repo: OK
deactivate DB
Repo --> Service: Qualification persisted
deactivate Repo

Service --> Controller: Qualification created
deactivate Service

Controller --> Operator: 201 Created + QualificationDTO
deactivate Controller

== UPDATE QUALIFICATION ==

Operator -> Controller: PUT /api/qualifications/{code} (QualificationDTO)
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: GetByCodeAsync(code)
activate Service
Service -> Repo: GetByCodeAsync(code)
activate Repo
Repo --> Service: Existing Qualification or null
deactivate Repo

alt Qualification Found
    note over Service
    Update the qualification name (if found)
    and persist the changes.
    end note

    Controller -> Mapper: ToDomain(dto)
    activate Mapper
    Mapper --> Controller: Updated Qualification
    deactivate Mapper

    Controller -> Service: UpdateQualificationAsync(qualification)
    Service -> Repo: UpdateAsync(qualification)
    activate Repo
    Repo -> DB: UPDATE Qualifications SET Name=...
    DB --> Repo: OK
    Repo --> Service: Updated
    deactivate Repo

    Service --> Controller: NoContent
    Controller --> Operator: 204 No Content
else Qualification Not Found
    Service --> Controller: null
    Controller --> Operator: 404 Not Found
end
deactivate Service
deactivate Controller

== SEARCH / FILTER QUALIFICATIONS ==

Operator -> Controller: GET /api/qualifications?code=&name=
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: GetAllAsync()
activate Service
Service -> Repo: GetAllAsync()
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: SELECT * FROM Qualifications
activate DB
DB --> Repo: List<Qualification>
deactivate DB
Repo --> Service: List<Qualification>
deactivate Repo

note over Service
Filters applied (if provided):
- Filter by Code (exact or partial)
- Filter by Name (case-insensitive)
end note

Service --> Controller: Filtered List<Qualification>
Controller --> Operator: 200 OK + JSON[List<QualificationDTO>]
deactivate Service
deactivate Controller

@enduml
